Here's the XAML and ViewModel setup:

## XAML

```xml
<RefreshView IsRefreshing="{Binding IsRefreshing}"
             Command="{Binding RefreshCommand}">
    <CollectionView ItemsSource="{Binding Items}"
                    SelectionMode="Single"
                    SelectedItem="{Binding SelectedItem, Mode=TwoWay}"
                    SelectionChangedCommand="{Binding ItemSelectedCommand}">
        <CollectionView.ItemTemplate>
            <DataTemplate x:DataType="models:MyItem">
                <Grid Padding="12" ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*">
                    <Image Source="{Binding Icon}" WidthRequest="40" HeightRequest="40" />
                    <Label Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding Name}" VerticalOptions="Center" />
                </Grid>
            </DataTemplate>
        </CollectionView.ItemTemplate>
    </CollectionView>
</RefreshView>
```

## ViewModel (using CommunityToolkit.Mvvm)

```csharp
public partial class ItemsViewModel : ObservableObject
{
    private readonly IMyApiService _api;
    private readonly INavigationService _nav;

    [ObservableProperty]
    private bool isRefreshing;

    [ObservableProperty]
    private MyItem? selectedItem;

    public ObservableCollection<MyItem> Items { get; } = new();

    public ItemsViewModel(IMyApiService api, INavigationService nav)
    {
        _api = api;
        _nav = nav;
    }

    [RelayCommand]
    private async Task Refresh()
    {
        var data = await _api.GetItemsAsync();
        Items.Clear();
        foreach (var item in data)
            Items.Add(item);
        IsRefreshing = false; // stops the spinner
    }

    [RelayCommand]
    private async Task ItemSelected()
    {
        if (SelectedItem is null) return;
        await Shell.Current.GoToAsync($"detail?id={SelectedItem.Id}");
        SelectedItem = null; // reset so user can re-select same item
    }
}
```

## Key bindings explained

| Property | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `IsRefreshing` (TwoWay) | Controls the refresh spinner; set `false` when done |
| `RefreshCommand` | Fires on pull-down; reloads data from API |
| `SelectedItem` (TwoWay) | Holds the tapped item; reset to `null` after navigation |
| `SelectionChangedCommand` | Fires when selection changes; triggers navigation |
| `ItemsSource` → `ObservableCollection<T>` | Ensures UI updates automatically on add/remove |

**Important notes:**
- Always use `ObservableCollection<T>`, not `List<T>`, so the UI reacts to changes.
- Set `SelectedItem = null` after navigating so the same item can be selected again.
- Set `IsRefreshing = false` at the end of your refresh logic to dismiss the spinner.
- Use `x:DataType` on `DataTemplate` for compiled bindings and better performance.
